---
description: A request to create a spec is read-only. The only write is the spec file.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Spec requests write only the spec

"Create a spec", "write a spec", or "new spec" is not permission to change the product.

1. Read the code and docs the spec depends on. Do not edit them.
2. Write only the spec file under `specs/`.
3. Stop.

Do not edit source, tests, config, Taskfiles, CI, lockfiles, AGENTS, README, or other specs. Do not install packages, run formatters, or generate lockfiles.

"Do it" or "it is time" in that request means write the spec. Implementation starts only when the user explicitly asks to implement that spec.
